WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.430
The colleague you work best with is the one who learned your preferences, your communication style and the things that annoy you.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.030
Why don't you teach your AI tool to be that colleague?

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.610
Because right now, you probably have the generic version of the tool.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.930
It's like a shared office chair.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.230
It works, but it's set for someone much taller.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.600
Sure, memory may pick up a few things.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:33.460
But standing instructions are something you choose: a short text, saved in your settings, that your AI reads before every chat.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.440
And a voice profile describes how you write.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:42.920
That turns the generic tool into one you enjoy working with, and you stop repeating your working preferences.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.660
So in this adventure, the AI interviews you and writes both.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.580
Then you test the same request, before and after,

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.680
until the new answer sounds like you.
